0 FILE 1210-2 - main.ldr
0 Alternate model of the 1955 set 1210, a small town-plan shop building assembled from white bricks, printed window/door elements, and geometric structural submodels.
0 Name: 1210-2 - main.ldr
0 Author: N. W. Perry [Plastikean]
0 !LDRAW_ORG Model
0 !LICENSE Redistributable under CCAL version 2.0 : see CAreadme.txt

0 !KEYWORDS slotted bricks, windows, doors, named beams
0 !KEYWORDS System i leg, town plan, set 210
0 !KEYWORDS shop, house, kiosk, 6 x 8

0 !THEME Town
0 // Release year: 1955
0 // No. of pieces: 30
0 // Four small sets, nos. 1210-1213, were released in 1955. Along with set no.
0 // 1236, these sets were the first to contain a selection of parts intended to
0 // build a specific model. They were also the first to have enclosed printed
0 // building instructions.
0 // The sets of this era were sold under the "System in play" concept, centered
0 // around the Town Plan building base layout. This is the original version of
0 // set 1210, with slotted bricks and windows and doors with tabs.
0 // * This set came with either a 1x6 or 1x8 brick, but not both as shown in
0 //   the instructions. This brick was printed with one of a wide variety of
0 //   names, in many different colours and languages.
0 // This is the alternate model for the set. The main model is a shop with no
0 // forecourt.
1 15 0 -8 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 u8203.dat
